WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:20.000
Governed Agentic Delivery: a briefing and pilot starter.
This silent walkthrough uses synthetic data, not a live agent.

00:20.000 --> 00:40.000
Platform teams need maintenance help without unrestricted access.
The goal is one useful, reviewable next action.

00:40.000 --> 01:00.000
The static website only presents HTML and local teaching fixtures.
It has no credentials, model calls, or repository writes.

01:00.000 --> 01:20.000
Real execution is separate: an approved trigger gathers bounded context.
The optional agent operates within configured tools and permissions.

01:20.000 --> 01:40.000
Repo Care asks for one low-risk maintenance improvement.
Untrusted repository text must not expand that written intent.

01:40.000 --> 02:00.000
Outputs remain staged. The example bounds turns, time, and AI Credits.
These limits are configuration, not measured usage or a price quote.

02:00.000 --> 02:20.000
Synthetic issue 101 asks for missing contributor test guidance.
The fixture's package.json supplies the existing test command.

02:20.000 --> 02:40.000
Preview the hand-authored expected decision.
The proposed documentation change is not applied.

02:40.000 --> 03:00.000
A maintainer must review scope, evidence, and real validation.
This replay has executed no tests or agent workflow.

03:00.000 --> 03:20.000
Now inspect the duplicate-work case.
Synthetic open PR 102 already addresses issue 101.

03:20.000 --> 03:40.000
The expected decision is no new proposal.
Review existing work rather than creating a duplicate.

03:40.000 --> 04:00.000
The insufficient-evidence case contains no supporting facts.
The expected result is no change: ask for a narrow reproduction.

04:00.000 --> 04:20.000
No-action results can be useful. Never invent evidence to force a patch.
All three cases are illustrative, not operational proof.

04:20.000 --> 04:40.000
Agree one pilot task, a repository owner, and a security reviewer.
Measure usefulness, reviewer effort, duplicates, usage, and cost.

04:40.000 --> 05:00.000
Confirm boundaries and stop conditions before optional execution.
Next step: complete the guide's scorecard and a go/no-go decision.
